<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">768 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">768 CE in world history: 2 events, 3 deaths and 1 state founded. 280 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/751">751 CE</a><a href="/years/756">756 CE</a><a href="/years/757">757 CE</a><a href="/years/763">763 CE</a><a href="/years/768" aria-current="page">768 CE</a><a href="/years/778">778 CE</a><a href="/years/787">787 CE</a><a href="/years/800">800 CE</a><a href="/years/822">822 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/desiderius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/desiderius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-31">31 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Lombard king Desiderius installs Philip as antipope for a day</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Intervening in the crisis after the death of Pope Paul I, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desiderius">Desiderius</a> seized a priest named Philip in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and had him appointed pope. Unrecognised, Philip left the same day and returned to his monastery.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desiderius">Desiderius</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-24">24 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pepin the Short dies, leaving the Franks to Charlemagne and Carloman</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">King Pepin died at Saint-Denis, dividing his kingdom between his sons Charles and Carloman, who were crowned in October. After Carloman's death in 771, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> ruled alone.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
